Diablo II Runeword Tracker
==========================

This project includes data derived from third-party work.

Runewizard
----------

The runeword, rune and base-item-category data in `src/data/` is derived from
Runewizard by Fabrice Denis, used under the MIT licence.

    Copyright (c) 2014-present, Fabrice Denis
    https://github.com/fabd/diablo2-runewizard

The unmodified upstream snapshot the data is generated from, together with the
full MIT licence text, is kept at `vendor/runewizard/`. The generator that
performs the derivation is `scripts/generate-dataset.ts`, run with
`pnpm data:build`; `docs/DATA-SOURCES.md` records the field mapping.

The files under `src/data/` are a transformation of that snapshot into this
project's own schema — renamed fields, normalised values, merged property
lines — and ship inside the deployed bundle. They are not verbatim copies, and
the attribution above travels with them.

Three visual assets under `src/assets/images/` are also derived from Runewizard
and used under the same MIT licence. Unlike the data these are byte-for-byte
copies of the vendored originals, since an image has no schema to transform
into:

    runes-sprite.png   all 33 rune icons in one 440x120 sprite
    mouse.png          the custom pointer
    hr-gold.gif        the ornamental divider band

Each is copied from `vendor/runewizard/assets/`, which keeps the unmodified
original alongside the MIT licence text. A test asserts the copies stay
byte-identical to those originals.

The reference project's own branding — its logo and wordmark — is deliberately
**not** reused. Those are its identity rather than a visual technique, and
reusing them would misrepresent this project as Runewizard.

Bellefair
---------

The display typeface in `src/assets/fonts/` is Bellefair, used under the SIL
Open Font License, Version 1.1. The full licence text sits next to the font it
covers, at `src/assets/fonts/OFL.txt`, and must stay there.

    Copyright 2015 The Bellefair Project Authors
    https://github.com/shinntype/bellefair

Only the latin subset is included, and it is self-hosted rather than loaded
from a font service, so the deployed page makes no third-party request.

